From 2d79de8d784e92f47ea849dc42f8153839a1b7d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:32:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gap-closing WIP: fuse the QSA prefill indexer score
 (QSA_SCORE_WMMA)

Port the AMD (RDNA3_5) 4-head/128-dim lightning-indexer WMMA kernel and use
ggml_lightning_indexer for qwen4exp's prefill indexer score: all-ones weights
+ a zero F16 mask reproduce the mul_mat + relu + head-sum chain in one op,
composed with the QSA_SCORE_BOUNDS causal trim (leading-rows key/mask views).

- lightning-indexer.cu: rename the entry points to *_generic, add the
  qsa_indexer_wmma16_keyreg kernel + supports_indexer4 (RDNA3_5), and add a
  generic vec fallback for n_head == 4 so the op is legal on every backend.
- qwen4exp.cpp: build the fused score for n_tps >= 128 / idx_dim == 128 /
  n_idx_h == 4, with the all-ones weights / zero mask shared per graph by name.
- test-backend-ops: add the nh=4 oracle cases (225/225 LIGHTNING_INDEXER).

Default ON.  Gated on gfx1151 qwen4exp IQ4_NL: op oracle 225/225 (81 new nh=4
cases); width_purity=PASS (worst maxdiff 0) with the per-W hashes byte-identical
to LLAMA_QSA_SCORE_WMMA=0 (the fused path is prefill-only, n_tps >= 128);
coherent same-seed text (a prefill re-baseline, wording-only difference);
pp32768 1311.5 -> 1324.9 t/s (+1.0 %, -b/-ub 8192) and 1265.9 -> 1277.2
(+0.9 %, -b/-ub 4096), pp8192 flat/within noise.  =0 restores the per-op chain.
